==English==

===Etymology===
{{L.}} ''{{l|la|bestialis|bēstiālis}}''.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/ˈbɛsʧəl/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[beast|Beast]]-like
# Of or referring to beasts
# Behavior motivated solely by instinct
# Like a beast in its lack of intelligence; [[brutish]], untaught, [[irrational]]; rude, [[barbarous]].
# Like a beast in obeying and gratifying the animal instincts and sensual desires; debased, [[deprave]]d, lustful, cruel, [[brutal]], beastly, obscene.

